I didn't run this prompt and wrote no `WORK_INSTRUCTIONS.md`, because it has no project gate. It starts with "Read ARBITER.md at this repository rootΓÇª" and has no `PROJECT: Hamlet` line. `CLAUDE.md` ┬º0.3.1 says a prompt without that line is not executed: the session says so and stops, and doesn't adapt it or apply part of it. `ARBITER.md` doesn't exempt the arbiter's prompt from that rule.

The problem is in the launcher. `.run-unit/arbiter-prompt.txt` starts with the same line, so every arbiter prompt it builds goes out without the gate. The fix is to make that template open with `PROJECT: Hamlet` and a blank line. Then rerun the loop; the redirect to 3.6 and 7.8 is still pending.

Separately, the Gmail, Google Calendar and Google Drive connectors need to be authorized in your claude.ai connector settings before they can be used. None of them were needed here.
